# caravan_abandon_witness.rish -- Caravan abandon witness.
#
# `confer.rye` closed the gap at the front of a dependent's life, `revoke.rye`
# the gap at the back of a standing one, and `reclaim.rye` the gap after its
# holder is gone. Three rungs about what a dependent may TOUCH. None of them
# asks what became of the WORK.
#
#   A CONFERRAL WHOSE HOLDER FELL SERVED NOBODY, AND THE RUN SAYS SO.
#
# A reclamation is silent about why its holder left. It takes the conferral
# back the moment the dependent is reaped, whether that dependent carried its
# work home or fell mid-arc, and both readings leave the same bare domain and
# the same clean count behind. Meanwhile the run has already counted the
# conferred phase as ABSORBED -- the record's word for taken up, which is its
# word for carried. So a plan whose author declared a fall reads back as a plan
# fully carried out, with an arc in it that nobody ever served.
#
# WHAT THIS RUNG PROVES, MEASURED:
#
#   * THE NUMBER THE TWO ROOMS DISAGREE ON IS ABANDONED REACH -- reach a run
#     conferred that nobody served, because its holder fell holding it. It is
#     the fourth of the family: dark reach was what a dependent could touch
#     before the door weighed it, stale reach what it could touch after its
#     work came home, inherited reach what a successor could touch at its first
#     breath. This one alone counts work that did not happen, and it falls from
#     1 to 0 the wrong way round: the silent run reports 0 while an arc is lost,
#     and the answering run reports the 1 that is true.
#   * EVERY OTHER NUMBER STANDS STILL, which is what makes the finding a
#     finding. Both runs take up 4 phases, spend 3 dependents, carry 1 home,
#     confer 1 arc, reclaim 1 conferral, and absorb 1 phase into a standing
#     dependent. Only the answer for the lost work moves.
#   * THE ANSWER STANDS ON THE WIRE, not in the supervisor's memory. The count
#     is written into the departed domain's own notes AFTER the reclamation has
#     swept them clean -- so it survives the very act that erases every other
#     trace of the conferral -- and it is read back before the report believes
#     it. A number an operator can read after the run is a fact; a number held
#     in a process that has exited is a claim.
#   * THE PLAN'S OWN DECLARATION REACHES THE DEPENDENT. A plan already names
#     the outcome it expects of every phase, and until now only the supervisor
#     read that word. The window this rung studies opens inside the dependent's
#     life -- after it grafts a conferral and before it carries the work -- so
#     the declaration rides the same wire as the pruning promise, written
#     before the spawn and read at the graft.
#   * FOUR REFUSALS THIS RUNG EARNS, EACH ABOUT WORK RATHER THAN REACH.
#     `AbandonStanding` is the moment: a dependent still in flight has
#     abandoned nothing, since it may yet carry every arc it holds.
#     `AbandonUngiven` is the supply: a dependent conferred nothing leaves no
#     work behind. `AbandonHomed` is the honesty of the count: a dependent that
#     came home served what it was granted, and a measurement that overstates
#     its own loss is as useless as one that hides it. `AbandonUncounted` is
#     the answer -- the hard half -- since a run that reclaimed a fallen
#     holder's conferral and recorded nothing would report an arc carried that
#     nobody carried.
#   * A RUN THAT ANSWERS FOR NO ABANDONMENT READS AS THE RUNG BELOW, all 9
#     pairs -- this arc's standing generalization test.
#
# All five RED paths were proven on metal before this witness claimed GREEN.
# Let the fold forget the moment and a standing dependent's work is called
# abandoned while it may yet carry it. Let it forget the supply and a run
# abandons work it never conferred reach for. Let it forget the honesty of the
# count and a dependent that came home is counted as having lost its work.
# Withhold the note and the run refuses its own record with `AbandonUncounted`
# rather than trusting a number it never read back. And answer under the wrong
# take, so the silent run counts 1 -- the guard catching the same gap from the
# other side, which is what proves it is a check rather than decoration.
#
# The first cut of the lap earned its own honest RED: the falling dependent was
# written second, the door refused it beside a standing sibling that contends
# over `board`, and the run passed its conferring phase ahead as a dependent of
# its own -- so the holder fell holding nothing, and the guard said so. The
# plan was reordered rather than the guard softened.
#
# Checks read the selftest output natively (`contains`), never a shell grep
# over interpolated output -- REDS %76 / %85, the apostrophe loom.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/caravan_abandon_witness.rish

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "caravan/bin/abandon"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p caravan/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/abandon.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]

assert build.ok else "caravan abandon build failed -- ${build.err}"

# The reader this witness runs is built here rather than borrowed (REDS %92).
let read_bin_build = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build caravan/read.rye -femit-bin=caravan/bin/read"]
assert read_bin_build.ok else "caravan read build failed -- ${read_bin_build.err}"

# The board declaration the rungs below opened, unchanged.
let published = run ["sh" "-c" "caravan/bin/read caravan/systems/serial_three_clients_board.bron 2>&1"]
assert published.ok else "the board declaration could not be read"
assert published.out contains "domains 4 -- channels 3 -- regions 11 -- grants 22" else "the board declaration changed shape"
assert published.out contains "verdict: whole" else "the board declaration did not read whole"

# A fresh provisioning each run, so every index starts at zero, every bell
# starts silent, and no dependent finds a conferral or an abandonment left by
# an earlier run.
let clean = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf caravan/.regions caravan/.channels caravan/.abandons"]
assert clean.ok else "the region stores, doorbells, and abandoning notes could not be cleared"

let test = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert test.ok else "caravan abandon selftest exited non-zero"
assert test.out contains "GREEN" else "caravan abandon selftest not GREEN"
assert test.out contains "a conferral whose holder fell served nobody, and the run says so" else "the abandon finding did not close"

# The abandonment and its three standing refusals, read straight, before any
# dependent runs. The fourth, `AbandonUncounted`, belongs to the run rather
# than the fold, since only the wire can answer whether the count landed.
assert test.out contains "a conferral buys work, and a run answers for the work it never bought" else "the abandonment fold was not weighed"
assert test.out contains "three refusals stand by name: standing, ungiven, homed" else "the three standing refusals did not stand"
assert test.out contains "the answer this rung reads: a conferral whose holder fell served nobody" else "the answering take was not named"

# The generalization test: a run that answers for no abandonment reads as the
# rung below.
assert test.out contains "a run that answers for no abandonment reads as the line handed, all 9 pairs" else "an unanswered run did not read as the line handed"

# The abandon lap: one plan run twice, once taking each fallen holder's
# conferral back in silence and once answering for the work it never bought.
# Every number but the last stands still, which is what makes the last one a
# finding rather than a difference between two different runs.
assert test.out contains "phases: 4 in silence, 4 answering" else "the two answers ran different records"
assert test.out contains "dependents: 3 in silence, 3 answering" else "the two answers spent different dependents"
assert test.out contains "carried home as handed: 1 in silence, 1 answering" else "a dependent did not come home as it was handed"
assert test.out contains "reach conferred: 1 in silence, 1 answering" else "the two answers conferred different reach"
assert test.out contains "conferrals reclaimed: 1 in silence, 1 answering" else "the two answers reclaimed different conferrals"
assert test.out contains "phases absorbed into a standing dependent: 1 in silence, 1 answering" else "the two answers absorbed different phases"
assert test.out contains "abandoned reach, conferred and never served: 0 against 1" else "the silent run and the answering run agreed about lost work"
assert test.out contains "breaks a named turn: 0 in silence, 0 answering" else "the answering run broke an order its author named"

# The dependents measure the finding in their own hands. The holder that falls
# says how much conferred reach it carries into the fall; the holder that comes
# home says nothing of the kind, because there is nothing to say.
assert test.out contains "falls as its author declared, holding 1 conferred arcs it never served" else "the falling dependent did not fall holding its conferral"
assert test.out contains "client_b: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 1 conferred, 0 returned, 1 still reachable at home" else "the dependent the conferral was made to did not read it as its own"
assert test.out contains "client_a: read 3 arcs of its own, 0 inherited at its first breath, 0 conferred, 0 returned, 0 still reachable at home" else "the dependent that came home read a conferral it was never made"

say "GREEN: Caravan abandon witness passed."
